DependencyEngine: SDD

Purpose:
  Define the internal dependency graph engine of the .sdd system itself —
  how dependencies are represented, validated, evaluated, and how they
  interact with the state machine, scheduler, and policy engine. This is
  NOT the project's concrete dependency graph (that lives in project/
  dependencies/), but the reusable rules and algorithms any project
  applies.

Owns:
  .sdd/dependencies/

Components:

  GRAPH:
    path: ./graph.sdd
    role: Dependency graph model (DAG, nodes, edges, types, metadata,
      cycle detection, topological sort, readiness calculation, failure
      propagation). Root-level, because this is reusable system
      intelligence, not project-specific state.

  LOCKING:
    path: ./locking.sdd
    role: Resource locking model (pessimistic/optimistic locks, leases,
      timeouts, deadlock detection, lock recovery, AI task collision
      prevention). Root-level, reusable system intelligence.

  PROJECT_GRAPH:
    path: ../projects/sddra.ai/dependencies/graph.sdd
    role: Project-specific dependency graph (concrete nodes, edges,
      states). Project-level, because this is concrete project state.

  PROJECT_LOCKS:
    path: ../projects/sddra.ai/dependencies/locks.sdd
    role: Project-specific lock state (active locks, reservations,
      conflicts). Project-level, concrete project state.

  PROJECT_RESERVATIONS:
    path: ../projects/sddra.ai/dependencies/reservations/
    role: Resource reservation instances. Project-level, concrete state.


Relationships:

  TASK
    -> GRAPH

  GRAPH
    -> STATE
    -> POLICY
    -> LOCKING

  LOCKING
    -> STATE
    -> POLICY

  PROJECT_GRAPH
    -> PROJECT_TASKS
    -> PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE


Allowed:

  TASK:
    may_reference:
      GRAPH

  GRAPH:
    may_reference:
      STATE
      POLICY
      LOCKING

  LOCKING:
    may_reference:
      STATE
      POLICY

  PROJECT_GRAPH:
    may_reference:
      PROJECT_TASKS
      PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE


Forbidden:

  GRAPH:
    must_not:
      bypass STATE for transitions
      mutate arbitrary state
      execute tasks directly

  LOCKING:
    must_not:
      bypass POLICY for lock acquisition
      bypass STATE for lock transitions
      execute tasks directly

Note:
  Created as dependency graph engine
  entry point. Root .sdd/dependencies/ = reusable system intelligence
  (graph algorithms, locking rules); .sdd/projects/sddra.ai/dependencies/ =
  concrete project state (actual dependency graph, lock state).
  ROOT-001 separation principle enforced.

State: +
